    "notes": {
        "third_party_runtime_dependencies": "None. There is no Composer, no npm, no framework and no CDN. The application is plain PHP with PDO, and plain JavaScript in the browser.",
        "platform_dependencies": "PHP 8 with the PDO, pdo_mysql, json, mbstring, openssl and gd extensions, and MySQL 5.7 or later. These are supplied and patched by the hosting provider, and are the only components for which a vulnerability announcement needs to be watched.",
        "why_this_matters": "A vulnerability in a library the application does not have cannot affect it. The list of things to watch is therefore PHP itself, the MySQL server, and the web server."
    },
